    "news": {
      "text": "**Macro**\n- US headline CPI rose to 3.7% from 3.4% and core to 2.6%, both above expectations, with more than three-quarters of the rise from energy. [nasdaq.com, 16 Oct 2026]\n- Fed Chair Warsh did not signal an October move, and October hike odds fell to below 15% from about 27%. [zackeiseman.substack.com, 16 Oct 2026]\n- Producer prices also came in above forecasts this week. [finance.yahoo.com, 16 Oct 2026]\n\n**Equities**\n- The S&P 500 fell 1.09% to 7,659 and the Nasdaq Composite fell 2.14% on Friday, led by chip and AI stocks. [investrade.com, 16 Oct 2026]\n- Concerns about a China chip threat and AI spending weighed on the AI trade, and the Nasdaq-100 fell 5% on the week. [nasdaq.com, 16 Oct 2026]\n- I found no earnings or guidance news for NVIDIA, Apple, Microsoft or Tesla in the last 24 hours.\n\n**Commodities and FX**\n- US oil rose above $100 a barrel after the Houthis attacked Saudi Arabia, including Aramco's \"nerve center\". [nasdaq.com, 16 Oct 2026]\n- Iran stepped up attacks on ships in the Strait of Hormuz, and a short-lived Russia-Ukraine \"energy ceasefire\" ended. [nasdaq.com, 16 Oct 2026]\n- Brent settled at $109.86. [financefeeds.com, 17 Oct 2026]\n- I found no gold supply news. Gold is not covered here because the sources I found were price commentary.\n- Yen: nothing notable. I found no intervention or policy news.\n\n**Crypto**\n- Nothing notable. I found no structural news for bitcoin or ether.\n\nNote: my search quota ran out partway through, so the yen, crypto and single-stock searches were not completed. Treat those \"nothing\" entries as unconfirmed.",
